  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1120 AM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nThe heat will stick with us through the start of next week. A Heat \nAdvisory remains in effect through Sunday for heat indicies of 105+. \nA trough will move through Tuesday that will allow for better, more \nwidespread rain and thunderstorm chances to return to the forecast.\nThe troughing pattern looks to remain in place through the week \nwith long range guidance hinting at a strong upper low dipping \ndown over the southeast. Should this happen, we would finally see \na pumpkin spice-esque change in our temperatures. The NBM is also\noptimistic with highs in the upper 70s to low 80s by the end of \nnext week and overnight lows in the upper 50s to low 60s....Yes, \n50s and 60s!! We'll continue to monitor 500mb long range trends \nand keep our fingers crossed that this pattern shift is on the \nway.",
